{"id":"n1-170","title":"Verbる べく","romaji":"Verb-ru beku","jlptLevel":1,"shortExplanation":"Expresses the meaning of 'in order to', 'for the purpose of'.","longExplanation":"The 'Verbる べく' grammar point is used to indicate a strong intention or purpose of the speaker. It can be translated as 'in order to' or 'for the purpose of' in English. It is more common in written language or formal contexts.","formation":"Verb-dictionary form + べく","examples":[{"jp":"成功するべく、日々努力しています。","romaji":"Seikou suru beku, hibi doryoku shite imasu.","en":"In order to succeed, I am working hard every day.","words":[{"surface":"成功","vocabId":"1375690","reading":"せいこう"},{"surface":"する","vocabId":"1595910","reading":"する"},{"surface":"べく","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"べし"},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"日々","vocabId":"1602120","reading":"ひび"},{"surface":"努力","vocabId":"1445130","reading":"どりょく"},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"い","vocabId":"1158500","reading":"い","baseForm":"いる"},{"surface":"ます","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[2]},{"jp":"健康を維持するべく、毎日運動をしています。","romaji":"Kenkou o iji suru beku, mainichi undou o shite imasu.","en":"In order to maintain my health, I exercise every day.","words":[{"surface":"健康","vocabId":"1256170","reading":"けんこう"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"維持","vocabId":"1158450","reading":"いじ"},{"surface":"する","vocabId":"1595910","reading":"する"},{"surface":"べく","vocabId":null,"baseForm":"べし"},{"surface":"、","vocabId":null},{"surface":"毎日","vocabId":"1524720","reading":"まいにち"},{"surface":"運動","vocabId":"1172910","reading":"うんどう"},{"surface":"を","vocabId":null},{"surface":"し","vocabId":"1310720","reading":"し","baseForm":"する"},{"surface":"て","vocabId":null},{"surface":"い","vocabId":"1158500","reading":"い","baseForm":"いる"},{"surface":"ます","vocabId":null},{"surface":"。","vocabId":null}],"patternWordIndices":[4]},{"jp":"彼は学位を得るべく、毎日勉強しています。","